### What other people told them or did

This tag counts reported advice or actions by people other than the focal child, including named co-caregivers; it does not treat an unspecified “we” as evidence of another person’s separate action.

- "I've gone to the pediatrician for this and at least in my country (Mexico) while they do tell me he should've been weaned off of it by now the societal norm is for them to keep taking at least night bottles until they decide to stop." [ar051-0060]
- "So everyone keeps telling me not to stress about it and that he'll eventually stop, that their kids had a bottle until 5-7 years old and their teeth were fine but my husband has awful teeth genetics he has had to spend a fortune on adult braces and cavity issues so I'm very concerned." [ar051-0061]
- "I've given him just water in his bottles (tip from my mom) and he didn't care, he just wants his bottle." [ar051-0062]
