- "I've attempted to feed, as has my husband and my mother." [ar030-0109]

### What they bought or paid for

Only one yes post explicitly reports buying something for this feeding problem, so there is one purchase quote rather than five. Using a brand or owning feeding equipment is not counted as payment; “got some nipple shields” does not specify buying them. The husband’s adult dental spending is reported context, not a purchase for the child’s feeding problem.

- "I've bought easily over 50 different types of cups, even smaller versions of my water bottle but he just. wants. the. freaking. bottle." [ar051-0062]

### How they say they feel

This tag counts feelings explicitly named by the parent, including curiosity and hope; requests for advice, wishes to change feeding and feelings attributed only to the child do not by themselves qualify.

- "Thankfully, he has not choked yet, but I’m so terrified he will." [ar032-0027]
- "Every other no I can take. A no for meals makes me panic." [ar079-0037]
