# Digest 09: pattern 7, Learning to eat and drink as a skill

Share: baby-development/_work/2026-11/digests-age-reread/share-09.md. Yes posts: 18. Near posts: 4.

## Pattern 7, share 09: yes posts

### The parent wants to teach straw drinking after attempts have failed.

2 of 18 posts.

These parents describe children aged 2 and 2.6 years who have not learned to drink through straws. One has moved from bottles to sippy cups and is approaching open-cup use; the other still uses a bottle for water despite trying yogurt and liquid trapped in a straw. They want ways to teach the skill, rather than simply omit straws.

- "I already tried the yogurt method, the one where you put water in the straw and putting your finger over the top of the straw to trap a small amount of liquid inside. But I still cant teach my son to use straw." [ar029-0054]
- "So far our attempts to teach him have left him frustrated and we have better success with open cups than straw cups but we dont want to skip straws entirely." [ar069-0003]
- "My son is already 2.6 years old and still uses bottle to drink water." [ar029-0055]

**But:** nothing found against it.

